  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "D.Nadarajan vs The Food Safety Officer on 24 April, 2024 Crl.O.P.(MD Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 24.04.2024 Coram: The Hon'Ble Mr Justice A.A.Nakkiran Crl.O.P.(MD)No.18126 of 2022 and Crl.MP(MD)Nos.12121 & 12125 of 2022 D.Nadarajan ... Petitioner / Accused No Vs. The Food Safety Officer, Code No.109 & 120, Chellampatti & Vadipatti Taluk, Designated Officers Office, Multipurpose Health Supervisors (F) Training School, Viswanathapuram, Madurai 625 014. ... Respondent / Complainant Prayer:Criminal Original Petition is filed under Section 482 Cr.P.C for the records and quash the proceedings in S.T.C.No.667 of 2021 o file of the learned Judicial Magistrate, Vadipatti, insofar as the concerned.",
    "facts": "The Food Analyst had sent a report on 19.10.2020 stating that the sample was substandard. The Designated Officer had sent the report of the Food Analyst along with his notice, dated 28.10.2020. The petitioner filed an appeal before the Designated Officer under Section 46(4) of the Food Safety and Standards Act in Form VII. But, in this case, the Designated Officer had not disposed this appeal and also not forwarded the one part of the sample to the referral laboratory and thus, violated the Food Safety and Standards Act as per Rules 2.4.6. The Food Analyst had sent a report on 19.10.2020 stating that the sample was substandard. Thereafter, the Designated Officer had sent the report of the Food Analyst along with his notice, dated 28.10.2020. After receiving the report, the petitioner filed an appeal before the Designated Officer under Rule 2.4.6(1) and Section 46(4) of the Food Safety and Standards Act.",
    "arguments": "3. The learned Government Advocate (Crl.Side) appearing for the respondent submitted that the petitioner ought to have filed an appeal to the Designated Officer in Form -VIII instead of Form VII and hence, he objected to quash the proceedings."
  },
